  "recipeDetail": "Comments from the Creator\nThe \"CineBiasOffset\" look features a subtle, cinematic color grading with a cool, muted tone. The overall palette leans towards soft blues and greens, creating a calm and introspective mood. Skin tones have a natural appearance but with a slightly de-saturated warmth that blends into the cool ambiance. Shadows are gentle, adding depth without overpowering the scene. This look feels refined and understated, ideal for narrative work where a natural yet cinematic vibe is desired.\n\nWhen using this recipe, we recommend setting [Active D-Lighting] to [Extra high] or [Extra high 1] on your camera. Selecting either of these options preserves details in highlights while achieving rich, cinema-like tonal gradations in your image.",
